<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sigebert I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 535–575</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sigebert I was the Merovingian king of Austrasia from 561, when the kingdom of his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I</a> was divided among his sons, until 575. He married the Visigothic princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunhilda-of-austrasia">Brunhilda</a>, and her rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fredegund">Fredegund</a>, wife of his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilperic-i">Chilperic I of Neustria</a>, fuelled a long civil war. He was assassinated at Vitry, reportedly on Fredegund's orders, at the moment of victory over Chilperic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sigebert-i.jpg" alt="Sigebert I" width="164" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lavisse, Ernest, 1842-1922 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sigebert_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
